Offline Concurrent Streaming Morse Decoder
Context
You are implementing an offline Morse decoder. The decoder receives chunks of boolean signal samples from any thread. true means tone is on. false means silence.
Chunks are analyzed on background worker threads. Worker results may finish out of order. The decoder must commit analyzed chunks safely, merge runs across chunk boundaries, and expose decoded text from the longest contiguous analyzed prefix of the signal.
The hard part is concurrency correctness: chunks can arrive out of order, worker jobs can finish out of order, clear() and setTiming() can happen while jobs are running, symbols can cross chunk boundaries, and snapshots must never block on workers.
